        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "会 (huì) is inherited from Middle Chinese hwajH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), glossed 'to come together'. The sense 'can' is not given there, so how it got it is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "会 + a verb says you have learned to do it: driving, a language, a skill. A sījī huì kāichē: a driver can drive. You have written 会 since 一会儿; this is another word in the same character."
            }
          ]
        },
